Article 14 The presidium shall handle the following matters:
(1) decide on the daily agenda based on the session agenda;
(2) decide on the deadline for deputies to propose bills during the session;
(3) hear and deliberate on reports on the handling of bills, and decide whether bills proposed during the session shall be placed on the session agenda;
(4) hear and deliberate on reports from the secretariat and relevant special committees on the deliberation and examination of various bills and reports, and decide whether to submit the bills and draft decisions and draft resolutions to the session for voting;
(5) hear explanations from the standing presidents of the presidium on the list of candidates for the composition of state organs, nominate candidates for the composition of state organs to be elected by the session, and determine the list of formal candidates in accordance with legal procedures;
(6) propose draft methods for election and decision on appointment during the session;
(7) organize the constitutional oath-taking by the members of state organs elected or appointed by the session; and
(8) other matters that shall be handled by the presidium.

Article 25 The Chairman, Vice-Chairmen, and Secretary-General of the Standing Committee shall form the Council of Chairpersons, which shall handle the following important day-to-day work of the Standing Committee:
(1) decide on the duration of each meeting of the Standing Committee, draft the meeting agenda, and, when necessary, propose adjustments to the agenda;
(2) decide, with respect to bills and questions submitted to the Standing Committee, to refer them to the relevant special committees for deliberation or to submit them to a plenary meeting of the Standing Committee for deliberation;
(3) decide whether to submit bills and drafts of decisions and resolutions to a plenary meeting of the Standing Committee for voting; for those not to be submitted for voting, propose next steps for handling;
(4) adopt the annual work priorities, legislative work plan, supervision work plan, work plan for deputies, special work plans, and work normative documents of the Standing Committee;
(5) guide and coordinate the day-to-day work of special committees; and
(6) handle other important day-to-day work of the Standing Committee.

Article 37 The work of each special committee shall be as follows:
(1) deliberate on bills referred to it by the presidium of the National People's Congress or the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress;
(2) submit to the presidium of the National People's Congress or the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress bills that fall within the scope of the functions and powers of the National People's Congress or its Standing Committee and are related to the committee, and organize the drafting of bills and other draft bills;
(3) undertake specific work related to the hearing and deliberation of special work reports by the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress;
(4) undertake the specific organization and implementation of law enforcement inspections by the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress;
(5) undertake specific work related to special inquiries by the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress;
(6) in accordance with the work arrangements of the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress, hear special reports from relevant departments of the State Council, the National Commission of Supervision, the Supreme People's Court, and the Supreme People's Procuratorate, and make suggestions;
(7) conduct investigations and research on issues within the scope of the functions and powers of the National People's Congress or its Standing Committee that are related to the committee, and make suggestions;
(8) deliberate on administrative regulations, decisions, and orders of the State Council, orders, directives, and rules of the departments of the State Council, supervisory regulations of the National Commission of Supervision, local regulations, decisions, and resolutions of the people's congresses and their standing committees of provinces, autonomous regions, municipalities directly under the Central Government, cities divided into districts, and autonomous prefectures, decisions, orders, and rules of the people's governments of provinces, autonomous regions, municipalities directly under the Central Government, cities divided into districts, and autonomous prefectures, autonomous regulations and separate regulations of autonomous areas, regulations of special economic zones, and interpretations of specific legal issues by the Supreme People's Court and the Supreme People's Procuratorate that are considered to contravene the Constitution or laws and are referred to it by the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress, and provide opinions;
(9) deliberate on questions referred to it by the presidium of the National People's Congress or the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress, hear the replies from the questioned organs, and when necessary, report to the presidium of the National People's Congress or the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress;
(10) study and handle suggestions, criticisms, and opinions from deputies, and supervise the handling of relevant suggestions, criticisms, and opinions;
(11) conduct foreign exchanges in accordance with the arrangements of the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress; and
(12) other work assigned by the National People's Congress and its Standing Committee.
